title: Cisco IOS-XR: OSPFv3 neighbors of all VRFs (SSH)
agents: cisco_xr_ospf
catalog: app/cisco
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 Monitors the OSPFv3 neighbors of all VRFs and processes of a Cisco IOS-XR
 router. The data is collected by the special agent "Cisco IOS-XR OSPF
 neighbors (SSH, all VRFs)", which runs "show ospfv3 vrf all neighbor" on the router via SSH.
 Password authentication needs "sshpass" on the Checkmk server; the password
 is read from the Checkmk password store and never passed on the command line.

 The service state follows the OSPF neighbor state: FULL and 2WAY are OK,
 DOWN is CRIT and all transitional states (ATTEMPT, INIT, EXSTART, EXCHANGE,
 LOADING) are WARN. All of these can be changed with the rule "Cisco IOS-XR
 OSPF neighbors (per VRF)", which also allows lower levels on the neighbor
 uptime (to detect flapping adjacencies) and the state for a neighbor that is
 missing from the output (default CRIT).

 The summary shows state (with DR/BDR role), address, OSPF process and
 uptime. VRF, neighbor ID, interface, priority and dead time are in the
 details.

item:
 The VRF, the neighbor router ID and the local interface, e.g.
 {default 10.255.0.2 on GigabitEthernet0/0/0/0}.

discovery:
 One service is created for each neighbor found in the output.
